---
title: Plain rolldown
summary: The plugin uses only standard build hooks, so it also works in a plain rolldown build. Set up one output file per source file and the .ts declarations, which tsdown would otherwise give it.
related:
  - tsdown-plugin-svelte/overview
  - tsdown-plugin-svelte/options
---

tsdown runs on [rolldown](https://rolldown.rs), and the plugin uses only standard build hooks, so it also works in a plain rolldown build. This setup was tested with rolldown 1.2.16. You set up the two things tsdown would otherwise give it:

- **One output file per source file**, so a component's `./util.ts` import finds `./util.js` beside it: `preserveModules` with `preserveModulesRoot: 'src'`.
- **Types for your `.ts` files**: [rolldown-plugin-dts](https://github.com/sxzz/rolldown-plugin-dts), the plugin tsdown uses. This plugin only adds the `.svelte.d.ts` files.

```ts title=rolldown.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'rolldown';
import { dts } from 'rolldown-plugin-dts';
import { svelte } from '@ogygia/tsdown-plugin-svelte';

export default defineConfig({
  input: ['src/index.ts', 'src/util.ts'],
  external: ['svelte', /\.svelte$/],
  plugins: [dts(), svelte()],
  output: {
    dir: 'dist',
    format: 'esm',
    preserveModules: true,
    preserveModulesRoot: 'src',
    entryFileNames: '[name].js'
  }
});
```

List every `.ts` file a component imports in `input`, so each one is built to its own file. Set the plugin's `out` to `output.dir` if that is not `dist`.

The plugin ships components; it does not compile `.svelte` files into an app. For that, use `@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte` or `rollup-plugin-svelte`.
